    }
    ```

    ## Oracle verification of Phase B, 2026-11-20 18:10: accepted as a milestone; Phase C next
    - Checked: 15 signed commits d949b0eb8..b1da37bf1 on origin/main; `phase-b-link-land.log` shows `LANDED b1da37bf1c`; harness `0b9c2e85` (Close transforms) on harness main. Spec sha256: python-charts.den `428dee3e...` and canvas.md `a34c7317...` equal the approved bytes; svg-renderer.den differs from `60841c3b...` only in the two authorized note links (diff read).
    - **Next, in this seat:** Phase C, starting with [[tasks/2026-11-20-transcript-inline-images]] (delegated to you as well): land the transcript image-preparation hook with the existing PNG resolver first, then extend it with `artifact:ID[:N]`, SVG and PNG artifacts as ruled above. A term landing (inbox) may be running; one gate machine-wide.

    ## Oracle ruling, 2026-11-20 22:20: Python display rows (harness touchpoint added)
    - Granted harness `src/frontends/gui/face_rows.rs` (in addition to the listed Phase C touchpoints): the Python cell row (`face_rows.rs:1464` -> `python_body`) calls the existing image-preparation hook **only for the image reference that `display()` emitted** (the returned `![[artifact:ID]]`/`:N`), per `specs/python-charts.den:97`.
    - Ordinary stdout, code fences, JSON and text that merely contain an embed string stay literal terminal rows; no Markdown rendering of general Python output.

    ## Oracle ruling, 2026-11-21 03:30: single-row Chrome hash refresh (under the operator's 2026-11-20 host-refresh approval)
    - Authorized: refresh only `matplotlib-layered/2x`'s Chrome and diff hashes and its measured fraction (frozen `6f5b9231...` 1.51582% -> fresh `ca9ecb2c...` 1.51649%) from this private capture. SVG and resvg bytes are identical; the row stays advisory; the advisory set stays the same 30 rows; every budget, tolerance and gate unchanged.
    - Separate signed commit naming old/new hashes and fractions; evidence `target/svg-handoff/chart-pinned-svg-reference-drift.json` cited in the report.
    - Any other row drifting, or a status change, stops and returns to the Oracle.

    ## Oracle ruling, 2026-11-21 07:45: land Phase C with `make land`
    - Authorized: `make land` on `f2b8eb380` (rebased). The required SVG/formal command, the 17 chart witnesses, test-boundaries and the exact-base gallery pass.
    - The two full-`make test` landing-fixture failures (stage-claim count `4 != 3`; QoS priority `20`) reproduce on exact base `a05e43aef` (`target/svg-handoff/chart-ci-{base,candidate}-control.log`): inherited, not caused by this diff; name them in the report. They go to `tasks/2026-11-19-full-gate-repairs`. Do not repair them in this task.
    - One gate machine-wide (rust-1-100 may be landing).


    ## Report from seat:01M7XBGWB3P8Y1NQD75NPPHT6Y

    [[Implement]] [[Done]] Phase C landed on origin/main at signed 57cc8e4e7. The lean gate passed all 2,434 selected tests, and the exact post-landing SVG and formal command passed all 987 model comparisons. All 17 chart witnesses passed and the 2,456-case paired gallery showed zero changed PNGs. Python display stores SVG revisions with exact source and data pins, and transcript, Markdown and canvas share the saved image. PNG artifacts are immutable. Removed duplicate exporter/font policy, document-only image budgeting and clip calculations. The report records earlier gate failures, configured retries and the upstream fixture repairs.

